<title>UK: Standard up as NatWest rates &quot;add&quot;.</title>
<headline>Standard up as NatWest rates &quot;add&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Standard Chartered Plc rose on Thursday in a weak overall market as analysts at NatWest Securities repeated an &quot;add&quot; rating on the stock, market sources said.</p>
<p>Analysts at the brokerage were not available for comment.</p>
<p>Standard shares, which have declined from the record 740p set on August 29, were up 10p at 660-1/2 by 1525 GMT.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
